   "source": [
    "# Setting up the data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The variables to extract should be passed as follows:\n",
    "- met_variables: a dict of meteorological variables, of format {\"var_name\":[list of levels], \"surface_var_name\":[]}\n",
    "- static_variables: a list of static variables to add. see `get_static_variables_functions` for a list of valid parameters, or add your own\n",
    "\n",
    "other parameters:\n",
    "- time_deltas (list of ints): met is extracted for eahc t-H hours, where H is each item in te list. t=0 (ie the time of the satellite measurement) is extracted automatically. time_deltas=[6,12] extracts the data at t=0, t-6h and t-12h.\n",
    "- return_asarray (bool, default=False): if false, returns as an xarray dataset. if true, loads into memory as a np array of shape (time, lat*lon, variables)\n"
   ]
  },
