    "can also get the inputs using the same function - note that at the moment, these regions have met only at 10magl (ie at a single level) and therefore should be treated like surface variables"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "inputs, names = get_square_satellite_inputs(mhd_dom, {\"Wind_Speed\":[], \"Temperature\":[]}, static_variables=[\"lat_coords\", \"topog\", \"landcover\", \"landcover_disaggregated\"], time_deltas=[100], verbose=True, return_asarray=False, return_variable_names=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Fixed domain data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "LoadDomainSatelliteData will load the data over a fixed domain in space, rather than centered around the release point. if we dont specify a domain, it will just load the maximum possible domain.\n",
    "You can otherwise specify the domain to cut, in latitude and longitude with domain_to_cut (see below)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "---- LOADING FOOTPRINTS\n",
      "Loading footprint data from /group/chemistry/acrg/LPDM/fp_NAME_pre20210701/SOUTHAMERICA/*BRAZIL*SOUTHAMERICA_201606*.nc\n",
      "reduced the number of datapoints by frequency 40\n",
      "Loading 48 footprints\n",
      "\n",
      " ---- LOADING MET\n",
      "Loading meteorology from /group/chemistry/acrg/met_archive/UM/SOUTHAMERICA/SOUTHAMERICA_Met_201606*.nc\n",
      "\n",
      "---- LOADING TOPOG\n",
      "trying to load topography from /group/chemistry/acrg/LPDM/topog_NAME/TopogUMG_Mk8_global.nc\n",
      "---- All done!\n",
      "-----CROPPING TO A FIXED DOMAIN\n",
      "cutting everything to the minimum possible domain: {'lat': [-60.981, 22.323], 'lon': [-91.329, -24.801]}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "met_args = {\"met_levels\":[3, 15]}\n",
    "data_dom = LoadDomainSatelliteData(year=\"2016\", region=\"BRAZIL\", month=\"06\", freq=40, verbose=True, met_args=met_args)#, domain_to_cut={\"lat\":[0,20], \"lon\":[20,40]})"
   ]
  },
